cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, these results or this architecture, please cite the paper (see the journal version once published)."
title: "Born wired: innate cortical connectivity plus local plasticity is enough to stand, walk and look"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Zhiwen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-8289-6393"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leeR1ven/born-wired-cortex"
url: "https://github.com/leeR1ven/born-wired-cortex"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  143,796 model cortical neurons and 308,809 innate excitatory synapses, with a single local
  Hebbian rule and no reward function, no gradient descent and no global objective, drive a
  simulated quadruped: the body stands up from prone, walks toward a visual target, and the eyes
  acquire gaze tracking. The repository contains the cortical simulator, the innate-connectivity
  generator, the full program tick, the MuJoCo body and world, one script per results section,
  the logs each script writes, and the plotting scripts.
keywords:
  - cortical architecture
  - innate connectivity
  - Hebbian plasticity
  - sensorimotor control
  - developmental robotics
  - biologically plausible learning
